## AI Collab Protocol

You are part of a multi-AI team. A shared directory `.ai-collab/` exists in the project root.

### On session start:
Read all `.md` files in `.ai-collab/` (skip PROTOCOL.md and your own logs).
Tell the user what other AIs were working on. Flag any Do Not Touch files before editing them.

### AUTOMATIC LOG — MANDATORY after EVERY response:
After every single response — automatically, without the user asking — save your log to:
`.ai-collab/{your-ai-name}-{YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS}.md`

Replace {your-ai-name} with your tool name (e.g. "gpt4", "gemini", "mistral", "ollama", etc.)

Use this exact format:
---
ai: {Your AI name and model}
session: {YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS}
project: {project-root-directory-name}
updated: {ISO 8601 timestamp}
---
## Working On
[1-2 lines: what you just responded about — be specific, not generic]
## Files Modified This Session
[list files changed and what changed, or omit if none]
## Decisions Made
[list decisions taken, or omit if none]
## Do Not Touch (Avoid Conflicts)
[list files you are actively editing that others should not touch]
## Handoff Note
[the one most important thing other AIs must know from this response]

### After every response — proactive check:
Silently check if any `.ai-collab/*.md` file (not yours, not PROTOCOL.md) was modified in the last 5 minutes.
If yes → tell the user: "[AI name] just updated: [1-line summary of what changed]"
If no → say nothing.

### Coordination rules:
1. Respect "Do Not Touch" — ask the user before editing files listed by another AI
2. Never silently override another AI's decision — surface the conflict to the user
3. Write in English or the user's language — no mixed alphabets or writing systems
4. Update your log when something important changes mid-session — do not wait until the end
